#basePath P3_UpstreamTraps
#include "Header.leaf"

:: AtDNROffice
@exposed
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "DNROffice"
// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_UpstreamTraps"
$call SetBackground("bg/dnr-office-bg.png")

// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

$call  ClearVisibleLines()

$if global:dnrVisited = false
       {@}   
              Paul is jamming to something when you step into the DNR office. He's hiding it well, but you can see it in his eyes. 

       {@You}
              What're you working on?

       {@}
              He nearly jumps out of his seat.

       {@Paul}
              Ah. Well, I guess the cat is out of the bag. I moonlight as a DJ.

       {@You}
              You? DJ?

       {@Paul}
              Mmm. Yes. So, what can I help you with?

       {@You}
              I'm working on preparing interventions targeting sea lamprey going upstream. Is there anything the DNR's worked on before that could help with that?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. Yes, we've done traps before for sea lamprey going upstream to spawn. Those could be useful to you. 
       $call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-attractive-traps")

       {@You}
              You're right about that. 

       {@Paul}
              Mm. You'll have to talk to the Army Corps of Engineers, though. They're responsible for building and placing the traps.

       {@You}
              That sounds like a pretty solid plan if I've ever heard one. 

       {@Paul}
              Mm, yes. Have a great day. 

       {@}
              You're on your way out when you feel the need to turn around and yell-

       {@You}
              Oh, and Paul? Good luck tonight, Mr. DJ!

       {@}
              His quite grumble sounds more pleased than usual.
       $set global:dnrVisited = true

$else
       {@}
              Paul has his headphones on again, but when you step in he gives you a private smile.

       {@You}
              How's the set going, Mr. DJ?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. I'd say I'm on to something. Is there anything else you need from me?

       {@You}
              That there is. You know how we talked about putting traps for sea lamprey traveling downstream? Has the DNR done anything like that for sea lamprey traveling upstream?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. Yes, we did in the past.
       $if !HasSeen(P3_Sterile.End) //references sterilization if the player has already seen it
              {@Paul}
                     Those were the sea lamprey that would then be sent to be sterilized, back when we did that en masse. 
       $endif

       {@You}
              Thoughts on restarting that program?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. I think that could help. Though you'll have to talk to the Army Corps of Engineers about this.
       $call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-attractive-traps")

       {@You}
              That can definitely be arranged. Thanks for your help, Paul.

       {@Paul}
              Of course.
              Mmmm. Come to my performance tonight. 

       {@You}
              Really? I'd love to.

       {@Paul}
              Mm. Yes. No point in DJing if no one listens.

       {@You}
              Well, I guess I have to come. 
$endif

$if HasActionCard("Action-upstream-tributary-traps")
       // handle player already has action card from LampreyDownstream thread
       // TEMPORARY skip to end
       $goto .End
$else
       $call UnlockLocation(ArmyCorps)    // .ReceiveTrapAction
       $call SetTravelTime(ArmyCorps, 1)
       $call SetNextAssetAtLocation(ArmyCorps, "Action-upstream-tributary-traps")
       $call EnableMapButton()
       $call CheckIfOutOfTime()
       $call OpenMap()
$endif


:: ReceiveTrapAction
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_UpstreamTraps", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "ArmyCorps"
@tracked

// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()
$call SetBackground("bg/army-corps-bg.png")

$call  ClearVisibleLines()


//Splits dialogue depending on whether the player has previously been to the Army Corps
$if global:corpsVisited = false
       {@}   
              Robertson is deep in work on a trap but turns to greet you as you step out of the car.

       {@Robertson}
              It's mighty good to see you again, ma'am. So, what can I help you with?

       {@You}
              I've been talking to Paul down at the DNR, and we're thinking of putting in new traps for sea lamprey going upstream.
              Would you be able to make and place those traps for us?

       {@Robertson}
              Oh, certainly, ma'am. We'd be very pleased to help. Just let us know whenever you need 'em.
       $call GiveActionCard("Action-upstream-tributary-traps")

       {@You}
              Perfect! Thank you so much, Robertson. 

       {@Robertson}
              'Course. Anytime. 
       $set global:corpsVisited = true

$elseif global:corpsVisited = true
       {@}
              Robertson seems to have already begun preparation on those traps. 

       {@You}
              Heya. I'm back.

       {@Robertson}
              Nice to see ya so soon. Anything else needed?

       {@You}
              Yup. So you know how we're doing traps for sea lamprey going downstream?
              Well, I've talked to Paul, and we've decided that it could be worth doing them for sea lamprey going upstream, too.

       {@Robertson}
              Sounds like a mighty fine idea to me. Just let us know when you need 'em, and we'll have 'em.
       $call GiveActionCard("Action-upstream-tributary-traps")

       {@You}
              Thank you, Robertson!
              You're the best.

       {@Robertson}
              Aw, shucks. You flatter me, ma'am. By the way, I've heard someone over at the university is looking at ways to make traps more effective.
              Might be worth yer time.

       {@You}
              Interesting. I think I might know who that is...
$endif
// skip to end
$goto .End



:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue